{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "At the Movies", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 5, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 9, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "A2.2", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Will, May, Might", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "We will go see a movie this weekend.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We might have to wait in line to buy tickets.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We may bring our own snacks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">'ll</span>.  </br></br>You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.  </br></br>The modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb.  </br></br>They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%). </br><span class=\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%).", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Quantifiers", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Are there any comedies playing?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "There are lots of movies to choose from.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I don't think we have enough options to pick from.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.</br></br> You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more</br> less/fewer</br> no/none </br>any/not any</br> some</br> a lot of/lots of</br> plenty of</br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount</br> a smaller number/amount</br> 0, nothing</br> ask about a number or amount/say there is no</br> a small number/amount</br> a very large number/amount</br> more than you need</br> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "drama", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a movie that is serious", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I prefer watching dramas.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "These are words you use to talk about movies.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "comedy", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a movie that is funny", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: If you want to laugh, you should check out this comedy.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "sci-fi", "type": "name"}, {"content": "short for science fiction; a movie about the future related to science ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Did you watch that sci-fi movie about the aliens?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "historical", "type": "name"}, {"content": "relating to the past", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I don't like watching historical movies. They're long!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "more or less", "type": "name"}, {"content": "sort of; to a certain degree", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: All the movies have more or less the same plot.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "storyline", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the main set of events in a movie; plot", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Some movies have interesting storylines.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "stuck", "type": "name"}, {"content": "unable to move from a particular position", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective) ", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We're going to be stuck in this line!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le09ob05aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Choose a movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of what happens in the movie. What's the storyline? What kind of movie is it?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Think of two different scenes from the movie. If you could change these scenes, what changes would you make?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write down your ideas. Use the words <span class=\"italic\">will</span>, <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your ideas aloud to your class.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I talk about movies.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about possible actions and events in a movie.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I talk about things that could happen.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0, "template_override": 1}, {"title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "engenn5le09ob05re2aud01", "images": [{"image": "engenn5le09ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 0, "time": "0", "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 1, "time": "100", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: There are plenty of movies to choose from! Dramas, comedies, sci-fi?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: What do you feel like watching?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Something funny!"}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob05re2img05.jpg", "id": 2, "time": "8500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Okay, that gives us fewer options to choose from. If you want to watch something funny, we'll check out <span class=\"italic\">Dinner at Mickey's</span>. It got lots of great reviews! Do you want to see that?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: I guess. All these comedies have more or less the same storyline anyways."}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob05re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "time": "26500", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Hm ... is there any kind of movie you don't want to see?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: No horror or historical movies.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Ok. If we don't decide soon, we may be stuck in this line for a while.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: You might want to stand in line then. We'll just check out <span class=\"italic\">Dinner at Mickey's</span>."}, {"image": "engenn5le09ob05re2img02.jpg", "id": 4, "time": "44000", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Okay.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Vanessa</span>: Are we going to have enough time to get tickets?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Marco</span>: Yeah, don't worry. I'll meet you over there."}], "coverimg": "engenn5le09ob05re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slidesh